+### Compact RoPE
+
+On single-device Qwen3.5-core text serving, `--kvmem-re-rope` uses the dense
+cache slots as RoPE positions in both Legacy and Layerwise recall. It supports
+`bf16`, `int8`, `fp8`, `rk8v4`, `rk4v4`, `rk4v4-e8`, `rk2v4-e8`, `nvfp4` and
+`k8v4` on the CUDA architectures that support inference in each format.
+The native page includes the normalized BF16 key. Pressure and Query restores
+rotate it at the new slot and encode it in the selected KV format. The
+stored V and V scales travel with the page. This also applies to the MTP cache
+and continuation. The option requires unscaled 64-dimensional Qwen RoPE with
+theta 1e7. The added BF16 key plane counts against both KV budgets in bytes.
 
 ### KVMem statistics extension
 
